The self-dogfood policy's exception declaration was bound to nothing.

Every other kind is tied to the change that cites it:
  guard:      the guard must be `required` in that commit's tree
  no-repro:   the test is executed and must FAIL at the parent
  not-a-fix:  the record must change with the declaration

exception: only checked that a record with that id existed somewhere in
history, so any commit could satisfy the gate by citing an unrelated
record. That is a declaration which is syntactically valid and
semantically false, which is the exact thing this gate exists to refuse.

Found by committing one: while landing the dogfood-policy toolchain fix,
the trailer first cited exception:environment-unreachable:rn-jest-react-
native-resolution, an unrelated record from an earlier push. The gate
accepted it. It was amended before pushing.

A real historical instance also exists on main:

  $ check-fix-policy.py --base 63c00cc --head 5dc6c42
  exit 0            (before this change)
  exit 1            (after)
  self-dogfood fix policy: 5dc6c424db9f: exception record
  validation/self-dogfood/exceptions/hidden-runs-contract.json is not
  touched by this range, so the declaration is not bound to this change.

A legitimate range, where the record is written alongside its citation,
still passes:

  $ check-fix-policy.py --base 5648d90 --head d7e996a
  exit 0
